     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Thank you for your quick answer!<br>I tried Chisq and it looks better for me.<br><br>Does OC scale the variance when the variance of the methylation level (numCs/coverage) within a group is bigger than assumed?<br>Or does overdispresion mean something else?<br><br>Thanks,<br>Ábel<br><br><br><br></span><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z3P-aam9dAo/WTbMK9tZjAI/AAAAAAAAAkg/OgBtFVwGFb8cmtwW1EI7TI-VEDvru95qwCLcB/s1600/wOC_chisq.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z3P-aam9dAo/WTbMK9tZjAI/AAAAAAAAAkg/OgBtFVwGFb8cmtwW1EI7TI-VEDvru95qwCLcB/s1600/wOC_chisq.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793232488901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3zND-4ti_Q7sXpLzU0ZoLm\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z3P-aam9dAo/WTbMK9tZjAI/AAAAAAAAAkg/OgBtFVwGFb8cmtwW1EI7TI-VEDvru95qwCLcB/s320/wOC_chisq.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"217\" border=\"0\"></a><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z3P-aam9dAo/WTbMK9tZjAI/AAAAAAAAAkg/OgBtFVwGFb8cmtwW1EI7TI-VEDvru95qwCLcB/s1600/wOC_chisq.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-z3P-aam9dAo/WTbMK9tZjAI/AAAAAAAAAkg/OgBtFVwGFb8cmtwW1EI7TI-VEDvru95qwCLcB/s1600/wOC_chisq.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793232488901000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3zND-4ti_Q7sXpLzU0ZoLm\"><br></a></p></div>"
